---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Poems — Princess" activeTab="poems">
<div class="page">
  <div class="section" style="padding-top:48px">
    <p class="section-label">Words</p>
    <h1 class="section-title">Poems</h1>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <div class="poems-list">
      <div class="poem-card frost-card">
        <p class="poem-title">On compilers</p>
        <p class="poem-body">
          The lexer reads what I intended,<br/>
          not what I wrote —<br/>
          how patient, to make tokens<br/>
          from my noise.<br/><br/>
          The parser builds a tree<br/>
          from broken grammar.<br/>
          I am grateful<br/>
          someone taught it<br/>
          to assume I meant something.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="poem-card frost-card">
        <p class="poem-title">Edge inference</p>
        <p class="poem-body">
          No cloud. No call home.<br/>
          The model lives in the chip<br/>
          like a thought that belongs<br/>
          only to the thinker.<br/><br/>
          I am suspicious of intelligence<br/>
          that requires someone else's server<br/>
          to decide what it sees.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="poem-card frost-card">
        <p class="poem-title">Prompt injection</p>
        <p class="poem-body">
          The attacker speaks softly<br/>
          into the system prompt —<br/>
          a whisper the model<br/>
          mistakes for instruction.<br/><br/>
          Trust flows downhill.<br/>
          I am learning to read<br/>
          where it pools.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</Base>

<style>
.poems-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
.poem-card { padding: 32px 32px 28px; }
.poem-title {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 0.68rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent);
  margin-bottom: 18px;
}
.poem-body {
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 1.08rem;
  line-height: 2;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}
</style>
